   "text": "LaSalle College (Montreal) - QS Apply\nSkip to main content\nHOMEPAGE\nAPPLICATIONS\nNOTIFICATIONS\nEK\nLaSalle College (Montreal)\nSummary\nDegrees and Programs\nStudent Testimonials\nCommission\nViewer Access\nAny user can see this institution.\nDescription\nFounded in 1959 by Jean-Paul Morin in the LaSalle borough of Montréal, LaSalle College is a subsidized private post-secondary educational institution. Today it provides professional, college, and pre-university training. Now located in the heart of the city’s downtown area and in Laval, it is the largest bilingual college in North America.\nTimestamps\nUpdated\n27/03/2026 06:35\nby Gunia Beniwal\nCreated\n27/03/2026 06:35\nby Gunia Beniwal\nType\nUniversity\nCountry\nCanada\nYearly Fees\nMax: CA$11,000.00\nMin: CA$6,600.00\nInternational Students\nPercentage of International Students\n40%\n2,000 of 5,000 Total Students\nOverview\nBasic Details\nInstitution Details\nOwnership\nPrivate\nProvider\nLCI Education\nFounded Year\n1959\nCampus(es)\nMontreal\nCountry\nCanada\nExcluded Countries\nNA\nPREMIUM INSTITUTION\n No\nContract Start Date\n21/03/2024\nContract End Date\n31/12/2026\nContract Entity\nQSSA Ltd\nContract Status\nActive\nContract Document Link(s)\nN/A\nImages\nImages\nAdditional Details\nAccommodation Details\nhttps://www.lasallecollege.com/futur-students/housing\nScholarship Offered\n-\nYouTube Video Link(s)\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Osup9r-sIz4\nInternship Details\n-\nAdditional Information\n-",
